@startuml sd-cqrs-query-read-model
skinparam style strictuml
autonumber
title SD - CQRS query side: local read model only (P2)

actor "ATCC" as User
participant "RouteController" as Ctrl
participant "RouteQueryService" as Query
participant "RouteReadRepository\n(route_read_model)" as RM

== Startup ==
note over Query, RM
  ReadModelRebuilder (CommandLineRunner, @Order(10))
  rebuilds airport_read_model and route_read_model
  from the write model: the read model is derived
  state and can always be reconstructed.
end note

== Query ==
User -> Ctrl : GET /api/routes/{id}
activate Ctrl
Ctrl -> Query : getRoute(id, hops)
activate Query
Query -> RM : findById(id)
alt found in this instance's read model
    RM --> Query : RouteReadModel
    Query --> Ctrl : RouteViewDTO (toView)
else not found
    Query --> Ctrl : 404 Not Found
    note right of Query
      No HTTP call to other instances
      (peer.forwarding.max-hops = 0).
      If the route was just created on another
      instance, it appears here as soon as the
      ROUTE_CREATED event is consumed
      (eventual consistency, ~1-2 s).
    end note
end
Ctrl --> User : 200 / 404
deactivate Query
deactivate Ctrl

note right of Query
  Query side never touches the write model:
  statistics, search, GeoJSON export and the
  BFS alternative-route search (FastestRouteStrategy)
  all read from route_read_model only.
  Commands go through RouteService (write model),
  which keeps the read model in sync via RouteProjector
  in the same transaction.
end note
@enduml
